{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f0156f1381b4f7c1","name":"Dagger-Class Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-f0156f1381b4f7c1","title":"Dagger-Class Starfighter","revision":19868,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:45:49Z","sha256":"a7e75d7a71fc342612d45f31cbf2ca0061a4179ef187cd46ad3fefaa5b8466d6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19868","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Dagger-Class%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f0156f1381b4f7c1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]},"-Class Space Superiority Starfighter is produced in large numbers by Republic Sienar Systems in the waning days of the Republic. It is a formidable craft for its time: small, maneuverable, and fast, with powerful weaponry and a relatively cheap price tag. It even incorporates a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," and a limited astrogation computer that stores enough data for three hyperspace jumps.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As with later examples of Sienar's design philosophy, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]},"-Class lacks shields or extensive life support systems. ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]}," pilots must don pressurized flight suits to withstand the rigors of space. An absence of inertial and gravity controls means that ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]}," pilots are also exposed to extreme gravitational forces as they dodge, weave, and careen through space.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Thousands of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]},"-Class Starfighters are produced by Republic Sienar prior to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},". The majority are purchased by planetary defense forces, and many of the systems that take up the banner of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}," have ",{"tag":"i","children":["Daggers"]}," in their arsenals. Given its low cost and ubiquitous nature, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]}," is also used by a number of mercenary organizations, as well as independent paramilitary contractors. The Trade Federation, in particular, contracts with a number of mercenary organizations that employ ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]}," Starfighters.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["With Republic Sienar's dissolution by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emperor Palpatine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emperor_Palpatine"},", and subsequent incorporation into the Republic Navy, production of many of its Starfighters ceases completely. This includes the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]},"-Class Starfighter. The design specifications of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]}," are eventually brought out for review by the newly founded Sienar Fleet Systems, and some elements of the class are incorporated into the initial TIE series of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dagger"]},"-Class Starfighter Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter